{#release-runbook}
@summary: End-to-end release runbook used by platform engineering
# Release Runbook

This runbook coordinates preflight checks, deployment steps, and rollback.

{#preflight}
@summary: Checks completed before deployment starts
# Preflight Checks

- Confirm CI is green.
- Confirm migration window is open.
- Confirm pager owner is assigned.
{/preflight}

{#deployment}
@summary: Controlled rollout steps for the service
# Deployment Steps

1. Deploy canary.
2. Monitor error budget and latency.
3. Promote to full rollout.
{/deployment}

{#rollback}
@summary: Recovery plan when rollout fails
# Rollback Plan

If canary fails, revert to last known good release and follow {@post-release-review}.
{/rollback}
{/release-runbook}

{#post-release-review}
@summary: Post-release checklist and follow-up tasks
# Post Release Review

Document incidents, open action items, and confirm metric stabilization.
{/post-release-review}
